1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
This walkthrough uses the sample file. Every figure you see is a sample number.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Start Here has three steps: Settings, Bills, then This Paycheck or the Dashboard.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,500
The Days 1-30 tab gives you one short task a day. Click a tab name to jump there.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:27,000
Type Yes in Done when a day is finished. The counter at the top keeps track.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Yellow cells on Settings start empty. Type your own next payday, pay schedule and take-home pay.

6
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:44,000
Pick USD or CAD and a date style. Leave Numbers to use on Auto.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:52,500
The example lives on the Sample tab. Look, but do not type there. It is never erased.

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:00,000
Type your bills on the Bills tab, in the empty yellow cells. Do not copy over the Sample tab.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,500
Day 5, One-Time: add costs that are not monthly, each with a date and an amount. These cells start empty too.

10
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:13,500
Next chapter: reading your paycheck plan.
